'''aftcastle''' (ȧft′kȧs-l), ''n.'' [< ''aft'' + ''castle.'' Cf. ''forecastle.''] ''Naut.'', an elevation formerly placed on the after part of ships of war, to aid in fighting.

'''after''' (ȧf′tėr), ''adv.'', ''prep.'', and ''conj.'' [(1) ''After'', adv., < ME. ''after'', ''æfter'', ''efter'', etc., < AS. ''æfter'', adv., after, afterward, back, = OS. ''aftar'', ''after'' = OFries. ''efter'' = D. ''achter'' = Icel. ''aptr'', ''aftr'' = Dan. Sw. ''efter'' = OHG. ''aftar'', ''after'' = Goth. ''aftra'', after, again, backward,

