'''after-image''' (ȧf′tėr-im″ạ̄j), ''n.'' An image perceived after withdrawing the eye from a brilliantly illuminated object. {{smaller|Such images are called positive when their colors are the same as those of the object, and negative when they are its complementary colors.}}

'''afterings''' (ȧf′tėr-ingz), ''n. pl.'' [< ''after'' + ''-ing-s''.] '''1.''' The last milk drawn in milking; strippings.
